ABOUT THE ROLE:
This role is a permanent full-time position.
As a plant shift Electrician, you will be responsible for routine maintenance, timely installation and where required, repair of equipment to ensure that plant related activities are executed in a safe manner, and that electrical reliability as per the requirements set forth by the supervisor, are met.
You will also be required to operate electrical equipment and test all working parts in functional area to ensure proper utilization.
Other key responsibilities include, but aren’t limited to:
Interprets and coordinates pre-work with regards to repairs, planned and predictive maintenance;
Accesses any area safely to perform necessary electrical maintenance on equipment;
Performs daily safety inspections of equipment and assesses risks on equipment;
Maintains a clean and safe worksite and accounts for the overall electrical reliability of the assigned section;
Work independently and in a team as well as under pressure;
Ensures the upkeep of maintenance tools and equipment;
Coordinates activities associated with trouble-shooting and repairing maintenance equipment;
Clear feedback to direct line Supervisor.
ABOUT YOU:
You will have experience and demonstrate capability in the following:
Must have a minimum of 3 years’ experience in electrical maintenance
Maintenance and fault finding on Allen Bradley VSD’s will be advantageous.
Medium voltage switchgear competence will be advantageous.
Plant experience (substations, MCCs, transformers, motors, liquid starters, safety circuits and switchgear (VCB/ SF6) ) will be advantageous.
MHSA knowledge/ experience will be advantageous
Qualifications for this role are:
Grade 12;
N3 trade certificate;
Electrician Trade;
Valid drivers license.
This advertisement will close on 15 December 2025
