About the job:
The CSIR has a vacancy for a
Senior Project Manager
in the Optronic Sensor Systems Impact Area, within the Defence and Security cluster.
The incumbent will be expected to work at tactical and operational levels of management to deliver on the impact areas mandate and strategy and apply project management expertise together with appropriate technical/domain/sector/industry specific technical acumen to achieve project goals by managing the total project management life cycle within project constraints according to applicable project management framework(s).
This is based in Pretoria and will report to the Research Group Leader.
Key responsibilities:
Initiate and manage projects by contributing to project proposals mainly from a financial perspective in terms of budget development and resource planning, ensure compliance to government requirements such as PFMA, ensure all project initiation documentation is in place and of appropriate quality;
Plan projects through coordination of resources required for project execution, assist with the development of project plans, also resource planning and implementation;
Execute, control and review project progress and expenditure;
Provide monthly financial reporting to project leaders and HR reports as necessary;
Assist with management and risk mitigation on projects, facilitate financial reports, liaising with stakeholders as necessary, balance constraints across and between projects;
Manage team and stakeholders (facilitate and negotiate), including communication (e.g. regular internal and external team meetings and progress reporting);
Close out projects in accordance with organisational processes and responsible for administrative closure of a project in terms of a project review, lessons learnt, financial closure of the project, project records and documents;
Play a major role in financial month and year end in preparing projects for funds declarations;
Assist on projects with any other issues they may face relating to health and safety issues, assets, procurement and marketing / engagement;
Work across geographical boundaries with multiple stakeholders.
Lead the development of technical project proposal, and Project Definitions;
Lead the development of Request for Proposal (RFP) and Expression of Interest (EoI) for SMME sub-contracting and selection process;
Plan and manage the project tasks and deliverables to align with the OSS set Key Performance Indicators (KPI).
Qualifications, skills and experience:
A Bachelors degree in computer/electronic/mechatronics/mechanical engineering, physics or mathematics with at least five years experience as a Project Manager, of which three years should be within the Defence and Security environment and/or Research Development Innovation (RDI) domain;
A post-graduate qualification or certification in project/technology/engineering management (e.g. PRINCE2/PMP) will be advantageous;
Must have:
Experience in mechanics or mechatronics or electronics or software development or modelling and simulation or Space Satellites/Aircraft/UAV payload engineering design;
Experience in all key component of Project Management such as resource planning, budgeting, reporting, and project artefacts;
Experience in working with project teams across organisational boundaries, under tight and dynamic deadlines;
Experience in Systems Engineering Management;
Experience in people management skills, soft and performance management;
Experience in leading teams with agile delivery;
A valid drivers license and existing or eligible for Department of Defence (DOD) security clearance;
Track record in managing complex research and development project (s);
Track record in contract management and financial management;
Knowledge of the electro-optical sensing systems development lifecycle;
Strong knowledge of Agile and Lean methodologies;
Adaptability to change, ability to multi-task and to consistently perform under pressure;
Good interpersonal skills and the ability to work closely with others across research groups;
Support business development and securing new contracts;
Support and manage the Industrialisation and Commercialisation projects;

Job Description
Media24’s Media Division is seeking an experienced Management Accountant. In this role you will be required to provide accurate and timely financial and accounting information to business unit managers to provide them with the basis to make informed business decisions.
This role will work across the areas of News both Digital and Print, Magazines, Content Marketing and Services.
This role is onsite and based at our Cape Town office and reports into the Financial Manager.
What You'll Do
Perform monthly financial reporting and analysis for business units and advise managers where required to ensure sound financial management;
Prepare business unit budgets and forecasts in liaison with managers where required;
Carry out financial report-writing requirements for relevant departments;
Monitor expenditure against budget and report on any deviances;
Ensure that designated business unit/department(s) is complying with all financial processes and procedures;
Investigate and resolve business unit/department financial queries;
Operate as a strategic link between business unit leaders and finance;
Responsible for business-unit internal and external audit interaction and query resolution;
Review and/or complete and submit all general ledger reconciliations with supporting documentation;
Prepare and review costing models and report variances;
What We're Looking For
Essential Requirements:
Education: B Com, CIMA or National diploma in accounting, cost and management, management, taxation, finance or internal auditing.
Experience: 2-5 years’ relevant experience.
Technical Skills: Financial analysis experience;
IFRS knowledge;
VAT knowledge;
Proficiency in all relevant software applications;
High level of proficiency in spreadsheet application, and all financial software required for reporting purposes.
Preferred Qualifications:
Articles
Industry Experience: Experience in the Media industry and Advertising agencies will be to your advantage
Key Competencies:
Strategic Thinking: Ability to interpret business challenges and recommend best practices
Communication Excellence: Strong verbal and written communication with influencing and negotiation skills
Personal Attributes: Trustworthy, analytical, detail-oriented, and ethical with strong judgment
Technical Proficiency: Expert in relevant financial software and reporting applications

Description
Manage day-to-day delivery of a specific digital product stream.
Manage the groomed backlog and sprint cycles of the individual digital products.
Own and refine the product backlog, ensuring designs and user stories are well-defined and prioritised.
Support sprint execution by clarifying requirements, through designs and user stories for the development team.
Provide creativity and out of the box thinking to solutions.
Translate the Product Manager’s vision and roadmap into actionable backlog items.
Align features and releases with roadmap milestones.
The list of tasks or duties and responsibilities herein is not exhaustive, and the employer is entitled to instruct the employee at any time to carry out additional duties or responsibilities, which fall reasonably within the ambit of the role profile, or in accordance with operational requirements.
Provide input into strategy by surfacing insights from team execution.
Collaborate with UX/UI teams to ensure customer journeys of the features are well supported and defined.
Validate product increments with users to ensure value delivery.
Track feature performance metrics and use data driven insights to enhance features.
Track sprint-level KPIs such as velocity, story completion, and defect rates.
Provide feedback loops from delivery into strategic planning for Product Manager.
Ensure team output ties back to product roadmap.
Conduct retrospectives post sprint with individual delivery teams.
Document user stories, acceptance criteria and workflows to build an accessible knowledge base.
Ensure backlog items are visible, transparent, and updated.
Create guides and training materials for cross-functional teams.
Ensure comprehensive documentation for each phase of feature development.
Build a knowledge base accessible across teams.
Facilitate Agile ceremonies (refinement, sprint planning, reviews, retrospectives).
Coordinate release planning and communicate project status, timelines, and any changes.
Identify blockers and work with the team to resolve them.
Streamline development processes to improve operational efficiency and reduce time-to-market.
Fulfil a cross-functional role by engaging and facilitating effective communication flow between different business units.
Ensure alignment of sprint goals with business priorities.
Provide transparency on progress, risks, and changes.
Develop instructional materials and support resources.
Facilitate continuous learning to keep teams updated on product developments and best practices.
Support training, adoption and smooth handover of new releases to business teams.
Requirements
Grade 12 or Equivalent (Essential);
Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science (BSc), Business Administration, or a related field (Essential);
Scrum Certifications (Advantageous);
4 years+ experience as Business Analyst or Product Owner (Essential);
Software projects and Digital solutions experience (Essential);
Knowledge of Agile methodologies;
Backlog management and user story mapping;
Tactical and detailed product lifecycle execution through sprint planning;
UX principles and acceptance criteria definition;
Practical knowledge of tools.
Personal Attributes:
Professional;
Able to handle sensitive and confidential information;
Organised;
Reliable and dependable;
Ability to work in a team and independently;
Internal and external networking;
Integrity and values;
Confidence;
Adaptive and Responsive.
