Purpose of the Job:
To manage all ICT assets (hardware and software) throughout their lifecycle to ensure assets are used effectively and according to organisational policies. The person appointed to this position will report to the ICT Services Manager.
Key Performance Areas:
Manage ICT assets (hardware and software) lifecycle from start to end, and ensure standards for the use and functioning thereof are adhered to;
Implement and maintain ICT assets policies and procedures;
Liaise with the FSCA Assets Management and Supply Chain functions to ensure ICT assets are managed according to organisational policies;
Administer the ICT assets register and report on assets status to management;
Manage ICT storerooms and asset disposals;
Coordinate ICT assets verification processes;
Monitor and record movement of all ICT assets;
Manage the software audit processes;
Keep record and track all software license keys;
Monitor supplier performance against agreed SLAs;
Manage loaner pools of computer assets;
Manage and coordinate asset warranties and guaranties;
Produce management reports on ICT assets; and
Provide support to the ICT teams on assets queries.
Enforce compliance to Occupational Health and Safety standards for ICT Assets
