The Minister of Agriculture, acting in terms of Section 5(1)(of the Veterinary and Para-Veterinary Professions Act, 1982 (Act No. 19 of 1982), has appointed a Selection Panel to identify and recommend suitable individuals for appointment as Ministerial Designees to the next South African Veterinary Council (SAVC), as prescribed by Section 5(1)(of the Act.
The Selection Panel has been mandated to select the following categories of candidates:
Two (2) persons on account of their knowledge of law;
Eight (8) veterinarians or veterinary specialists; and
Two (2) non-veterinarians.
APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS
Individuals wishing to be considered for appointment are invited to submit the following:
A letter of motivation indicating suitability for one of the above categories (c(i), c(ii), or c(iii));
A comprehensive CV;
Certified copies of all relevant qualifications; and
A certified copy of the applicant’s ID.
Members of the Council shall hold office for a period of three (3) years and will be eligible for redesignation thereafter.
ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA
To be eligible for selection, an applicant must:
Be a veterinarian or veterinary specialist, where required;
