Position Purpose
Leads the TPT Tactical Procurement department, across all areas of spend within designated portfolio with the goal of achieving significant initial cost reductions, with year-on-year productivity improvement in the total cost of goods and services procured while maintaining product quality and vendor service levels.
Develops and implements Tactical sourcing strategies to improve the efficiency of all tactical procurement events, demand management to contract management and close-out, while reducing the total cost.
To improve procurement governance and compliance, operational efficiency, costs savings and reputation management.
Position Outputs
Implement Tactical Procurement strategies and processes to deliver commercial outcomes for Transnet Port Terminals:
Formulate tactical procurement strategies to ensure successful implementation;
Facilitates proper demand management and forecasting to ensure security of supply;
Supports continuous improvement by seeking out efficient business solutions to improve processes in support ofoverall business strategy and direction;
Identify potential bottlenecks in tactical procurement and formulate plans to manage potential risks; and
Conduct training and awareness sessions in all applicable internal and external policies, regulations and laws thatimpact on tactical procurement and monitor and report on breaches and submit and implement recovery plans.
Participate in innovation and research of emerging trends in tactical commodities/associated industries to informprocess re-engineering.
